{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/760760-wraiths-from-9-11-and-iraqi-war","id":760760,"title":"wraiths from 9/11 and Iraqi war?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-08T10:53:52-08:00","id":760760,"title":"wraiths from 9/11 and Iraqi war?","content":"Just curious if this has been examined allready I think it would be interesting to look at... though I hope any A Q Leaders have been Smelted upon Reaping with considerable prejudice....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-08-2015, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:48:26-08:00","id":760805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/760760-wraiths-from-9-11-and-iraqi-war#post760760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious if this has been examined allready I think it would be interesting to look at... though I hope any A Q Leaders have been Smelted upon Reaping with considerable prejudice....</div> </div> </div> </div>No more than any other fanatic, I imagine. Human politics don't always carry over into Underworld politics. But there are a few options.<br /> <br /> I would say most 'Al-Qaeda' leaders (there's at least some doubt about them being a single organisation as opposed to a loose network of related groups) would die in the Middle East, where things would be much more up for interpretation than they would in the West. They'd be full of horrid thoughts and would probably be Shadow-Eaten straight out the Caul.<br /> <br /> Any extremists who die in the West would be mere tools for more powerful conspiracists (usually themselves based in the Middle East), but in my opinion would probably die thinking they had fulfilled a higher purpose because of the nature of their indoctrination. As such, they're likely to Transcend (it's not always about being a good person) or fall straight to Oblivion (they have no loose ends to tie up, because they literally think they're serving God and are off to a better place).<br /> <br /> If they didn't skip the Underworld altogether, I'm sure the weight of their crimes would drag them down into the Labyrinth as spectres too. There could be some quite nasty spectre cults that emerge from this.<br /> <br /> As Wraith ended in 1999, it doesn't go into the issue at all, so this is conjecture. However, I think Orpheus might mention the Shadowlands of New York?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-08-2015, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T12:52:06-08:00","id":760868,"title":"","content":"Post-6GM and 9/11 New York is covered in the Orpheus book End Game. The World Trade Center is... well, a place of sacred horror, a place where ghosts and projectors who enter find individual Harrowings, and potentially benefits for those who embrace the opportunity to face their inner darkness that Harrowings provide.<br /> <br /> Iraq? Can't speak for the official take, but I suspect the Middle Eastern Shadowlands are pretty turbulent right now, what with Daesh and Syria stirring things up - I can't imagine older wraiths in the area are particularly happy with what Daesh have been doing to the artifacts of the past, especially when some of those were probably Fetters. If Iraq is Stygian territory, then a lot depends on how capable the local Hierarchy is... and that's a big question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:24:16-08:00","id":761020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/760760-wraiths-from-9-11-and-iraqi-war?p=760868#post760868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post-6GM and 9/11 New York is covered in the Orpheus book End Game. The World Trade Center is... well, a place of sacred horror, a place where ghosts and projectors who enter find individual Harrowings, and potentially benefits for those who embrace the opportunity to face their inner darkness that Harrowings provide.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it. Thought I'd seen it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Iraq? Can't speak for the official take, but I suspect the Middle Eastern Shadowlands are pretty turbulent right now, what with Daesh and Syria stirring things up - I can't imagine older wraiths in the area are particularly happy with what Daesh have been doing to the artifacts of the past, especially when some of those were probably Fetters. If Iraq is Stygian territory, then a lot depends on how capable the local Hierarchy is... and that's a big question. </div> </div> </div>I think, in previous supplements, the Middle East is meant to be nominally Stygian. But that doesn't mean that it's Western wraiths ruling. They could very well be ancient Middle Eastern wraiths who are otherwise allied to the Dark Kingdom of Iron. If there's some kind of colonialism going on in the Shadowlands, that would no doubt add to the tension.<br /> <br /> The point about relics and sacred sites being destroyed is a good one, although it's likely an issue individual wraiths or groups might have, rather than the Hierarchy in general. The Hierarchs of the Middle East might benefit greatly from all the new relics pouring into the Shadowlands, which they can use to trade or build new citadels (especially important if the Sixth Great Maelstrom has hit in your game). Individual wraiths would be pissed, but the Hierarchy doesn't really get involved in Skinlands matters anyway--it just takes what opportunities it can to bolster itself against Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's no doubt plenty of nihils that have opened in the area now, too. Wraith: The Great War no doubt has some good material to mine for inspiration in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T02:00:40-08:00","id":761318,"title":"","content":"Aaaaand now I know what I'm going to touch on for Chapter Three of my little guidebook miniseries. Chapter two is below if you want a look. Thanks for the inspiration!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/758543-guidebook-to-stygia-chapter-two-entertainment-district\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/758543-guidebook-to-stygia-chapter-two-entertainment-district\"> Guidebook to Stygia, Chapter Two: Entertainment District - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/758543-guidebook-to-stygia-chapter-two-entertainment-district\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/758543-guidebook-to-stygia-chapter-two-entertainment-district </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> &amp;quot;Crikey! Look at the size of that one! Got way too many teeth in the wrong places, but if you know just the right spot to pet it'll calm right down&amp;quot; the </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:21:33-08:00","id":761425,"title":"","content":"The thing you have to remember when you consider how to handle wars, terrorism, or really anything in Wraith, is that being dead changes everything. <br /> <br /> You are not the same person you were when you died. And that's not a euphemism or a metaphor either; in Wraith, when you die all the complexity, identity, and self deception is scoured and subsumed until the core emotions keeping you here are laid bare to the world. Your Passions become quite literally your only reason for being and what you were in life becomes a lot less important than <i>why</i> you were, in life. <br /> <br /> It would not be unheard of for the ghost of the man who erected a monument, the ghost of a foreign soldier who died protecting it (and the people around it), and the ghost of a terrorist who blew himself up trying to destroy it, to unite in protecting a common fetter, or if the motivations were right, in advancing a common agenda. Likewise it would not be unheard of for the ghosts of a soldier with feelings of betrayal and the terrorist who killed him to join forces as renegades against the Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Culture, belief, and ideology played (and still play) a huge role in making Wraiths who they are, but are far from the only influence. Nothing unites like a common struggle and Oblivion, as they say, pulls on everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T10:27:52-08:00","id":761585,"title":"","content":"hmmmn just thought... would it be unreasonable, for a wraith who had one of the artifacts Isis shattered as one of his fetters... to take the terrorist now as his new fetter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:45:11-08:00","id":761919,"title":"","content":"Assuming they became wraiths, I imagine that quite a few members of Al Qaeda <i>et al</i> have ended up with various Heretic groups. They were &quot;fighting in the name of God&quot;, after all. Why would a little thing like death stop them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/760760-wraiths-from-9-11-and-iraqi-war?p=761585#post761585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn just thought... would it be unreasonable, for a wraith who had one of the artifacts Isis shattered as one of his fetters... to take the terrorist now as his new fetter?</div> </div> </div> </div>He'd have to cultivate hatred in his heart for IS/ISIS/ISIL/Daesh, until it became one of the defining elements of his personality. A Passion is a drive greater than death, a Fetter pulls stronger than Oblivion . . . just being really pissed at the guys who destroyed his old one isn't enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T13:54:23-08:00","id":763424,"title":"","content":"Dansky mentioned somewhere that Wraith20 will cover the Shadowlands of the Middle East and how they came to be part of Stygia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T16:41:06-08:00","id":763579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/760760-wraiths-from-9-11-and-iraqi-war?p=761919#post761919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming they became wraiths, I imagine that quite a few members of Al Qaeda <i>et al</i> have ended up with various Heretic groups. They were &amp;quot;fighting in the name of God&amp;quot;, after all. Why would a little thing like death stop them?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's if they didn't succumb to Oblivion upon finding out heir beliefs were... misguided. Of course, like some real-life apocalyptic fanatics, I could ask see them doubling down, claiming that they still need to be tested before they can achieve salvation. <br /> <br /> Which, of course, would put them squarely in the Heretics you mentioned.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}